# The output rail.
#
# Not the built-in `self check output`: that flow's action returns a yes/no, and
# a repair loop needs to know what was wrong. `verify_answer` is registered in
# guardrail.py and runs `verifier.Verifier`, which returns the problems it found
# alongside the decision. NeMo still owns the rail — when to run it, and what
# happens when it blocks.

# Overrides the message NeMo's own library defines. The stock text is
# "I'm sorry, I can't respond to that.", which tells a user nothing about what
# this system is for; a refusal is the only thing some users will ever see it
# say, so it may as well point them somewhere useful.
define bot refuse to respond
  "I can't help with that one. This assistant answers questions about the indexed arXiv papers — try asking about a method, a result or a figure in the literature."

define bot refuse to answer
  "The drafted answer did not survive checking against the retrieved passages."

define flow check answer grounding
  $result = execute verify_answer
  # Carried back to the caller through GenerationOptions(output_vars=...), which
  # is how the repair loop learns what to fix. The rail itself only decides.
  $verify_problems = $result.problems

  if $result.is_blocked
    bot refuse to answer
    stop
